'Swurls the Silent Clown' is a short silent film from Angelfreak Entertainment.  The film is separated into three segments, each featuring Swurls (played by K. Patrick Carpenter) performing a different slapstick charade.
ACT I: "Charades" - Swurls plays a game of charades with the viewer.
ACT II: "Tic-Tac-Toe" - Swurls plays a game of Tic-Tac-Toe with the viewer.
ACT III: "A Friendly Fly" - Swurls is pestered by a fly that just won't seem to stay put.